      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — Captain Toadette.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, hand-authored from the article. XP ledger: level 3, power rating 7 → a level 3 Fighter player-character sheet (a player may take this seat; the authored CR 3 stands in where the ledger is silent). Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>The Ruthless Restorer</strong> — Peach Loyalists</p><p>Status: Active — back from Warp Pipe Junction with dull claws and a closed question about rats</p><p>Captain Toadette is the military commander of the Peach Loyalists and the scariest person in the Mushroom Kingdom who isn't a dimensional horror or a kaiju. She plans operations with tactical brilliance, executes them with total commitment, and maintains a no-prisoners policy that would make the Iron Legion uncomfortable. Waluigi has arm-wrestled Bowser and felt LESS uneasy than he does contemplating Captain Toadette.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Restorer's Pick</strong> — “Captain Toadette is the military commander of the Peach Loyalists and the scariest person in the Mushroom Kingdom who isn't a dimensional horror or a kaiju.”</li><li><strong>Hand Crossbow</strong> — “Captain Toadette is the military commander of the Peach Loyalists and the scariest person in the Mushroom Kingdom who isn't a dimensional horror or a kaiju.”</li><li><strong>Extra Attack</strong> — “Captain Toadette is the military commander of the Peach Loyalists and the scariest person in the Mushroom Kingdom who isn't a dimensional horror or a kaiju.”</li><li><strong>Ruthless Restoration</strong> — “Captain Toadette is the military commander of the Peach Loyalists and the scariest person in the Mushroom Kingdom who isn't a dimensional horror or a kaiju.”</li><li><strong>Scarier Than Bowser</strong> — “Waluigi has arm-wrestled Bowser and felt LESS uneasy than he does contemplating Captain Toadette.”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/captain_toadette</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/captain_toadette</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
